% A constraint must observe its variables even when its type has a
% position some loop looks up by index. `X == 4` becomes an index
% condition on item's second argument, so item has an indexed position,
% but the store is far too small to be indexed yet. Binding V later must
% still reactivate item(1, V), so the rule fires.
:- module(reactivation_indexed_position, [start/1]).

:- chr_constraint p/1, item/2, fired/0, ask/1, start/1.

p(K), item(K, X) ==> X == 4 | fired.

fired \ ask(R) <=> R = 1.
ask(R) <=> R = 0.

start(A) <=> item(1, V), p(1), V = 4, ask(A).
